#
# One recipient's grant of a whole number of units split by weight
# (crown_rules.h CW2), in Sutra, one recipient per row: its floor,
# units * weight / total truncated as COMPUTE does, plus extra, the 1 the
# largest remainder gives it (0 when it gets none). The model works out
# total (the sum of the weights) and extra (the leftover units go one each
# to the largest remainders, a tie to the earlier recipient), and this
# answers with what it is given; allot.tb works both out again from the weights
# and refuses a total or an extra they do not give: held. units and the
# total fit 9(9): past them, or below 0, a size error, refused; a total of
# 0 divides by zero.
record allotment
  units: 9(9)
  weight: 9(9)
  total: 9(9)
  extra: 9
  floor: 9(9)
  grant: 9(10)
procedure
  compute floor = units * weight / total
  compute grant = floor + extra
  answer grant
